{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["And the reason for <b>\"And I shall be sanctified among the children of Israel\"</b> according to the opinion of our Sages (Torat Kohanim, chapter 9, halakhah 4) is that it is a positive commandment, that we sanctify His Name through the commandments — to be killed for them and not transgress. And this is the reason for \"who brought you out of the land of Egypt to be to you for Elohim,\" for this reason encompasses all the commandments, for it is fitting to sanctify His Name over them, because we are His servants whom He redeemed from Egypt."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:58:06.891366501Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}